A callback push on iPhone replaces the phone's own reminder for the same source.

Base: zan-workspace main at 8a8191c.
Apply from the web repo root:
    git apply --check /path/to/zanverse/docs/backend-patch/callback-collapse-id.patch
    git apply /path/to/zanverse/docs/backend-patch/callback-collapse-id.patch
    npx tsc --noEmit

What it changes:
- sendPush.ts builds apns-collapse-id in one helper, getCollapseId. Every channel keeps
  `<channel id>-<entityId>`, as today. A callback push now uses `callback-<sourceId>`.
  That is the id the phone gives its own reminder (zanverse src/lib/push/reminders.ts) and
  the id Android already uses for a callback push (zanverse src/lib/push/remoteMessage.ts).
  Before, iOS would have used `callbacks-<sourceId>`, so a server push and the reminder
  would show as two notifications on an iPhone.

Nothing sends a callback push yet, and the iOS app is not built. So nothing changes today.
No migration and no new environment variable.

